# Positive control -- NOT a false positive. THE critical regression-guard case for Bug D's
# redesign of looksLikeCodeReference (a per-segment identifier check, not a fixed
# root-prefix list): a genuine high-entropy secret that happens to contain literal dots (a
# JWT/base64-shaped value split into three dot-separated segments, e.g. a real JWT's
# header.payload.signature) must still be flagged. Each segment here is deliberately
# digit-dense and case-chaotic -- the exact opposite shape of a real identifier like
# "self"/"access_key" -- so isLowEntropyIdentifierSegment correctly rejects every one of
# them and the value is NOT treated as a code reference.

